{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-IMPLEMENTATION RESEARCH — three corrections to this ticket, all MEASURED against the pinned\ndependencies in this worktree (boto3/botocore 1.43.58, pydantic-ai-slim 1.107.1).\n\nCORRECTION 1 — THE ESCAPING EXCEPTION IS NOT A BARE NoRegionError, so this ticket's AC would pass\nVACUOUSLY as written. pydantic-ai already catches botocore's NoRegionError at\nproviders/bedrock.py:463 and re-raises `pydantic_ai.exceptions.UserError`:\n    \"You must provide a `region_name` or a boto3 client for Bedrock Runtime.\"\nMeasured with the env stripped of AWS_REGION/AWS_DEFAULT_REGION/AWS_PROFILE. So an AC asserting \"a\nTYPED error, not a bare NoRegionError\" is already true today and proves nothing. The REAL defect is\nnarrower and must be stated that way: `UserError` is NOT a subclass of rebar's `LLMError` /\n`LLMUnavailableError`, so no `except LLMError` handler in rebar catches it — including the review\nbot's fail-closed path — and its message names a pydantic-ai kwarg (`region_name`) rather than\n`REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION`. Rewrite the AC to assert the raised type IS `LLMConfigError` (hence\ncatchable by the existing fail-closed handling) AND that the message names the rebar setting.\n\nCORRECTION 2 — `AWS_REGION` ALONE DOES NOT WORK on this botocore, so the infra fix must not use it.\nMEASURED:\n    AWS_REGION=us-east-1 only      -> Session().region_name is None -> client() raises NoRegionError\n    AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=eu-west-1   -> Session().region_name == 'eu-west-1'\nbotocore's session-variable table (configprovider.py:74) maps region to AWS_DEFAULT_REGION only;\nAWS_REGION appears solely in smart-defaults auto-mode and as an endpoint-ruleset builtin. Two rebar\ndocstrings are INACCURATE about this and should be corrected as part of this ticket:\nbedrock_model.py:50-51 and config.py:19-20 both claim boto3 resolves \"AWS_REGION/AWS_DEFAULT_REGION\".\n\nCORRECTION 3 — the preflight oracle must be `boto3.session.Session().region_name`, NOT env sniffing.\nIt is a read-only property resolving the config-file key or the env var; no credentials, no network,\nno IMDS; measured at 0.002s. Hand-rolling `os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\")` would report a region that\nboto3 then refuses (per correction 2). Keep the boto3 import lazy inside the function, per this\nmodule's leaf-import contract.\n\nWHY IMDS IS IRRELEVANT HERE, now with the mechanism: botocore's IMDSRegionProvider is wired ONLY into\nthe smart-defaults path (defaults_mode=auto), so a reachable IMDS supplies credentials but never a\nregion. That confirms this ticket's \"two independent concerns\" claim at the code level.\n\nCOLLATERAL FINDING, worth folding into this ticket's value: the review bot's CloudWatch voter metrics\n(voter.py:95/110/151/215, four best-effort call sites) silently no-op for the SAME missing-region\nreason. Their comments blame IMDS reachability, which the above shows is not the cause. Setting the\nregion un-breaks voter metrics too — relevant because eb6e's rollback plan depends on a CloudWatch\nalarm firing on VOTER_ERROR.\n\nEXACT INFRA TARGET, with a precedent already in the tree: infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, service\n`review-bot`, environment block at :88-109. Two services below, the `opcert` service at :157-161\nALREADY sets the region with a comment diagnosing this identical failure (\"the region is not\nauto-discovered inside the container -> set it explicitly (else the job fails 'You must specify a\nregion')\"). Root cause of the asymmetry: infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh fetches the region from IMDSv2\nat :33-40 but only `export`s it into its own shell for the aws CLI calls; the `.env` it writes at\n:111-127 contains no region key. So fixing fetch-secrets.sh to emit the region is the alternative\nthat would cover both services.\n\nTEST HOME AND A TRAP: tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py section C (\"construction\"), right after\ntest_missing_bedrock_extra_raises_naming_the_install_command at :306 — same LLMConfigError import,\nadjacent shape precedent. The test MUST `monkeypatch.delenv` AWS_DEFAULT_REGION/AWS_REGION/AWS_PROFILE\nand set AWS_CONFIG_FILE to os.devnull, or a developer with ~/.aws/config passes it vacuously by\nresolving a real region. For the infra assertion, copy tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py:374\n(test_opcert_compose_service_sets_aws_region) one service over — and assert AWS_DEFAULT_REGION, per\ncorrection 2."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785466531186104001,"uuid":"85d2d352-dbf5-4cc8-bc58-37bf5570afeb"}